{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Problems and Solutions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Finally, We Got It!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.  Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.  Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Certainty About Conditions:<span class=\"italic\"> If </span>and <span class=\"italic\">When", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to talk about the certainty of a condition, you can use the first conditional with<span class=\"italic\"> if </span>and <span class=\"italic\">when. You use the first conditional to refer to events, actions or situations that are possible in the present or the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the first conditional, you have to be careful of which word (if or when) you use. The use of each implies a different meaning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If </span>you have some time this afternoon, will you please send me a copy of the confirmation? ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">If </span>implies a less certain meaning. In this sentence, the condition of <span class=\"italic\">If you have some time this afternoon</span> implies that the speaker is not sure if the person has some time.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I will send it to you <span class=\"strong\">when</span> I get back to the office.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">When</span> implies a more certain meaning. In this sentence, <span class=\"italic\">when I get back to the office</span> implies that the speaker is quite certain that they will return to the office.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take a look at some more examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If we provide itemized receipts, all other expenses will be covered as well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If we tip a cab driver, we won't really be able to get a receipt.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I suppose we will receive our conference badges when we check in, right?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Perfect Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Infinitives are a common grammar point to use in English. You can use them in a variety of forms and with different verbs. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the Perfect infinitive when the action of the infinitive has already taken place.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">seem to have enjoyed </span>your vacation. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The action (enjoy your vacation) took place in the past. The observer is noticing something about that event and is commenting on it in the present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The form of the perfect infinitive is:<br> verb +<span class=\"italic\"> to have </span>(in the infinitive form) <br><span class=\"italic\">  I'm <span class=\"strong\">glad to have made</span> your day, Adam.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We were smart to have submitted such a detailed proposal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Weren't we supposed to have heard about the conference by now? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It would be disappointing to have written that whole proposal only to have the request denied.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Kristi was supposed to have told you.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to look over ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to review", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Would you like to look it over?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to discuss a proposal.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to give something a once-over ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to review something quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Let's give it a once-over, just to make sure everything is in order.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "requisition ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to officially request something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Were all of our requisitions accepted?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go over with a fine-tooth comb ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to review something thoroughly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They really went over it with a fine-tooth comb.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "per diem ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an amount of money allotted for spending each day", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did we get our per diem?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "itemized receipt ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a detailed receipt which includes a full list of items purchased", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  If we provide  itemized receipts, all other expenses will be covered as well.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "autonomy ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the ability to act or make decisions without authorization", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I suppose, but they are giving us a great deal of autonomy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le12ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine that you will go on a trip with your entire class.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list including where you will go and what you will do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Estimate a price for each part of your trip (e.g. airfare, lodging, museum, etc.).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your proposal to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I plan a trip.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a detailed proposal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I project expenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my proposal to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can express that a fairly certain condition will be fulfilled in work and job issues.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express emotions and feelings related to work and job situations. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can exchange complex professional information related to work and job issues.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " If you have some free time this weekend, what will you do?